# This directory exists so a local Docker build can trust an extra CA
# certificate — e.g. a corporate proxy's or antivirus's TLS-inspection
# root cert, on networks where one transparently re-signs outbound HTTPS
# (pip installs against PyPI included). See apps/api/Dockerfile's builder
# stage for how this gets copied into the image's trust store.
#
# Drop your own *.crt file(s) here before building if `docker build`
# fails with "SSLCertVerificationError: unable to get local issuer
# certificate" — nothing else needs to change. Machine-specific, so never
# committed: everything here is ignored except this file.
*
!.gitignore
